  "scope": "For a block-permutation-invariant k-cell Hamiltonian of bounded per-cell norm sum, a sign-independent rounding argument selects symmetric ground sectors with exchange strength independent of block size and volume. Applied to the actual supplied tensor cubic with a three-cell guard, it proves occupation control and the fixed-volume Gaussian limit. A two-helicity gravitational constraint phase, Einstein quartic, nonzero physical coupling limit and TOE remain unproved."
